ℒc​o​l​o​r=∑k=1Kwk⋅min⁡‖Ct​e​x−Cm​i​l​i​t​a​r​yk‖22\mathcal{L}_{color}=\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}\cdot\min\|C_{tex}-C_{military}^{k}\|_{2}^{2}

where wkw\_{k} is a dynamically adjusted weight according to the target deployment environment. By minimizing the distance between the generated texture and the reference color schemes, this loss enforces global tonal consistency with the surrounding background. The minimum-distance formulation allows different regions of the texture to align with different dominant colors, thereby capturing the natural color variations commonly observed in real-world environments.

